---
import AppShell from '../layouts/AppShell.astro';
---

<AppShell title="Directory" description="Turn local businesses with a public phone into a calling board. Search any place on earth. Free for 100 leads. No credit card." withRoom>
  <section class="guest-sale" data-guest-sale>
    <header class="sale-intro">
      <p class="sale-kicker">A calling tool, not another map tab</p>
      <h1>Stop hunting Google Maps for businesses to call.</h1>
      <p class="sale-lede">
        If you sell to local shops, you already know the loop. Open Maps. Click a pin.
        Hope they have a number. Copy it into a note. Forget who you already rang.
        Do it sixty more times. Directory is that job, finished: a map of real local
        businesses anywhere on earth, and a board you actually work from.
        Free searches the whole world. No credit card.
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="sale-window" data-sale-window>
      <figcaption class="sale-window-bar">
        <span>Directory</span>
        <span class="sale-place-row">
          <span data-sale-place>Opening a market…</span>
          <button type="button" class="sale-reroll" data-sale-reroll>Another city</button>
        </span>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="sale-window-body">
        <aside class="sale-rail" aria-label="Listings in view">
          <div class="listings-head">
            <p>In view</p>
            <span class="listings-count" data-sale-count>0</span>
          </div>
          <div class="listings-track sleek-scroll" data-sale-list>
            <p class="listings-empty">Opening a live market…</p>
          </div>
        </aside>
        <div class="sale-map-stage">
          <div class="map-canvas" data-sale-map></div>
          <div class="map-zoom">
            <button type="button" class="map-zoom-btn" data-map-zoom-in aria-label="Zoom in">+</button>
            <button type="button" class="map-zoom-btn" data-map-zoom-out aria-label="Zoom out">−</button>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="map-search-here" data-search-here hidden>Search this area</button>
          <p class="map-scan" data-map-scan hidden>Scanning this area…</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </figure>
    <p class="sale-caption">
      This is a live city, picked at random from Canada or the US. The pins and the
      cards are real local businesses with a public phone — name and number, ready
      to dial. Refresh, or tap Another city, and you land somewhere else. Join free
      and search your own market.
    </p>

    <div class="sale-block">
      <h2>What you are looking at</h2>
      <p>
        Directory does not dump every restaurant, bus stop, and apartment building onto
        a map. It pulls businesses that publish a name and a phone — the ones you can
        actually ring. You get them as a list you can call, not as a place you have to
        visit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Search any place on earth — a city, a street, an address. Filter by niche — barbers,
        dentists, gyms, lawyers, salons, trades — or take everything in view. Move the
        map, hit Search this area, and the list refreshes for that viewport. Name and
        phone sit on the card. Hours, site, and the map listing are one tap away.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="sale-beats">
      <li>
        <span>01</span>
        <h2>Find a market, not a pin</h2>
        <p>
          Search a city, a street, even a single address. The map centers there and
          zooms until at least five businesses with a public phone are in view. You are
          not hunting pins. You are opening a market.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>02</span>
        <h2>Save without copying anything</h2>
        <p>
          Tap plus. That listing lands in New with the number already on it. Same
          card you saw on the map — name, phone, city, type. Nothing pasted into
          Notes. Nothing lost in a spreadsheet named “leads final v3.”
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>03</span>
        <h2>Call, then move the card</h2>
        <p>
          Six stages: New, Contacted, Responded, Meeting, Proposal, Won. Drag as
          you work. The phone stays on the card so you can dial from the board.
          Paid accounts skip the one-by-one grind and import a city once a day.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <figure class="sale-window sale-window-board">
      <figcaption class="sale-window-bar">
        <span>Leads</span>
        <span>The same cards, on a board</span>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="sale-board" data-sale-board>
        <p class="listings-empty">Live cards from the city above land here.</p>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <div class="sale-block">
      <h2>On every listing</h2>
      <p>
        A lead is useless if you still have to look the number up. Directory keeps
        the calling facts on the card and the rest in the sheet.
      </p>
      <ul class="sale-facts">
        <li>
          <strong>Name and phone</strong>
          <span>On the card. Copy or tap. That is the whole point.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Open or closed</strong>
          <span>So you do not dial a shop that shut at five.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hours, site, and maps</strong>
          <span>One tap into the listing sheet.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Type, city, rating</strong>
          <span>Enough to know who you are ringing before you ring them.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sale-split">
      <div>
        <h2>If you are just getting started</h2>
        <p>
          You do not need a CRM or a data vendor to make twenty honest calls this week.
          Join free. Search any place on earth — a city, a street, an address.
          Plus the shops you want. The board holds 100 leads. No credit card.
          No trial that turns into a bill.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>If you run a team</h2>
        <p>
          Paid is the same product with the ceiling taken off. No lead cap. Once
          every 24 hours you import one city — a single niche, or every niche in
          that city — and the pipeline fills with numbers ready to dial. That is
          how an agency works a market instead of nibbling at it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sale-block">
      <h2>Why this is not just Google Maps</h2>
      <div class="sale-compare">
        <div>
          <h3>Google Maps</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Built for getting you to a place</li>
            <li>Mixes shops with parks, stops, and homes</li>
            <li>You copy numbers by hand</li>
            <li>No memory of who you already called</li>
            <li>No board, no stages, no import</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Directory</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Built for calling a market, anywhere</li>
            <li>Businesses with a public phone</li>
            <li>Phone is already on the card</li>
            <li>Plus saves it to your pipeline</li>
            <li>Six stages, and a city import on Paid</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sale-plans">
      <article class="sale-plan is-free">
        <p class="sale-plan-kicker">Anywhere on earth</p>
        <h2>Free</h2>
        <p class="sale-plan-price">$0</p>
        <p class="sale-plan-blurb">
          Tokyo, Lagos, Manchester, or the street you grew up on. Same map. 100 leads. No card.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Search any place on earth</li>
          <li>100 leads on your board</li>
          <li>Add listings one at a time with plus</li>
          <li>Name, phone, hours, site on every card</li>
          <li>No credit card</li>
        </ul>
        <button type="button" class="btn-primary hover-lift" data-leads-pick="free">Join free</button>
      </article>
      <article class="sale-plan">
        <p class="sale-plan-kicker">One city a day</p>
        <h2>Paid</h2>
        <p class="sale-plan-price">$9 <span>a month</span></p>
        <p class="sale-plan-blurb">
          For agencies that need a market in the pipeline before lunch, not a pile of pins.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Everything in Free</li>
          <li>No lead cap</li>
          <li>Import one city every 24 hours</li>
          <li>One niche, or every niche in that city</li>
          <li>Oracle drafts a next call — it never sends</li>
        </ul>
        <button type="button" class="btn-glass hover-lift" data-leads-pick="paid">Join paid</button>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="sale-close">
      <h2>Open a city. Start calling.</h2>
      <p>
        Free takes a minute. You get the globe, the list, and a board that holds
        100 leads — any place on earth. When the city is too big for plus, Paid fills it for $9 a month.
      </p>
      <button type="button" class="btn-primary hover-lift" data-leads-pick="free">Join free</button>
    </div>
  </section>
</AppShell>
